    "diseaseAccession": "DI-05935",
    "acronym": "MC4DN14",
    "description": "An autosomal recessive mitochondrial disorder with onset in early childhood. MC4DN14 is characterized by developmental delay, cognitive impairment, motor delay, abnormal gait, sensorimotor demyelinating polyneuropathy, exercise intolerance, obesity, and short stature. Serum lactate levels are marginally increased. Patient tissues show decreased levels and activity of mitochondrial respiratory complex IV.",
